    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "The Israel Defense Forces strikes southern Beirut, Lebanon, for the first time since November 2024, after projectiles were fired from Lebanon. ((CNN))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "A Russian drone attack on Dnipro, Ukraine, kills four people and wounds 19 others. Multiple buildings in the city are reported to be ablaze, including a hotel, resort, a restaurant complex and numerous apartments. ((Reuters))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "At least seven people are injured by U.S. military airstrikes in the Yemeni capital Sanaa. ((Euronews))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "An under-construction government office skyscraper collapses in Bangkok, Thailand, killing at least six people and leaving more than 101 others missing and trapped under the rubble. ((CTV News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "A 7.7 magnitude earthquake strikes Sagaing, Myanmar, with significant damages reported as far away as Bangkok, Thailand. Over 1,000 people are killed in Myanmar and ten more in Thailand. A state of emergency is declared by the Myanmar government. ((CNN Live)) ((NBC News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "The Ava Bridge in Mandalay Region, Myanmar, partially collapses as a result of the earthquake. ((News18))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "Russian authorities say that yesterday's sinking of the Sindbad submarine in Hurghada, Egypt, killing six Russians, happened during boarding and not due to a collision as reported. ((The National))"
    },
    {
      "category": "International relations",
      "text": "U.S. Vice President JD Vance and several other senior Trump administration officials visit the Pituffik Space Base, a United States Space Force facility in Greenland. ((NPR))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Law and crime",
      "text": "Turkish authorities detain Mehmet Pehlivan, a lawyer representing opposition leader Ekrem İmamoğlu in the ongoing investigation, and later release him. ((Reuters))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "The Israel Defense Forces strikes southern Beirut, Lebanon, for the first time since November 2024, violating the ceasefire agreement.((CNN))"
    },
